FILED s536f (Opus 5.5, 2026-11-08) while fixing #4341 (scratch/s536f/p/m1g.pl in the s536f worktree).  PRE-EXISTING: main c8886b61 answers the same.

REPRODUCER (probed vs perl 5.40.3):

    my @a = (1,2,3); my %h = (k => 5); my $x = 7;
    for ((@a)[0]) { $_ = 9 } print "1 @a\n";
    for ((@a, $x)[3]) { $_ = 8 } print "2 $x\n";
    for ((%h)[1]) { $_ = 6 } print "3 $h{k}\n";
    for ((($x, 1), 2)[0]) { $_ = 4 } print "4 $x\n";
    sub w { $_[0] .= "w" } w((@a)[1]); print "5 @a\n";
    w(((@a), 1)[2]); print "6 @a\n";

perl: `1 9 2 3` / `2 8` / `3 6` / `4 4` / `5 9 2w 3` / `6 9 2w 3w`.   PCL: `1 9 2 3` / `2 7` / `3 5` / `4 7` / `5 9 2 3` / `6 9 2 3`.

WHY (read, not fixed): two halves.  (a) a raw-slot `my $x` in the list is lowered as its VALUE -- `(p-aref-deref (vector @a $x) 3)` -- so there is no box to alias; the foreach / argument veto (VarAnnotator `_ev_foreach_alias_list`, the arg-to-writer event) does not look inside a list slice.  (b) a single-index list slice is `(p-aref-deref LIST i)`, which answers the element's VALUE (p-aref); a sub argument / foreach slot needs the element CELL (as `(p-aref-deref-box ...)`, which since s536f #4341 reads a VECTOR index as the slice whose elements are already the slots' cells).  Row 1 works because the one-array list unwraps to the array itself.
BAR: the reproducer as a guard row beside #4341's in Pl/t/list-slice-01.t.


